WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.590
- Welcome back to "The
Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:04.110
I'm your guest host for
today, Howie Mandel.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.520
With me is my friend

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.650
from "America's Got Talent Superstars,"

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:08.483
Terry Crews,
(audience cheers)

00:00:08.483 --> 00:00:11.940
as well as my beautiful
daughter and co-host

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.440
of "Howie Mandel Does Stuff"
podcast, Jackie Schultz,

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.920
and like all children do eventually,

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.320
Jackie is now going to
take control from me,

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.120
so go ahead Jackie.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.580
- Thanks, dad, if that's your real name.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.610
So anyways, it is time for a
game that celebrates families

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.670
and all the wonderful nepotism
that goes along with them.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:36.030
This is called Famous Family Funtimes.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:37.536
- [Howie] Woo!
(audience cheers)

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:40.949
♪ Famous Family Funtimes ♪

00:00:40.949 --> 00:00:41.820
- (laughs) Okay.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.650
- All right, so here's how it works.

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.671
I'll read a sentence that
includes two first names

00:00:46.671 --> 00:00:47.880
of famous people.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.210
One is a parent and the
other is that parent's kid,

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.860
and what you guys have to do

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:55.947
is give me the last
name that connects them.

00:00:55.947 --> 00:00:57.731
- Oh?
- Oh, okay.

00:00:57.731 --> 00:00:58.920
- All right.
- Okay.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.750
- First clue, they're stars
of stage and stars of screen.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.984
Their names are Martin and Charlie--

00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:08.680
(buzzer rings)

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:09.954
- Sheen!

00:01:09.954 --> 00:01:14.954
(bell dings)
(audience cheers)

00:01:14.988 --> 00:01:16.443
You gotta hit the button.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:18.810
- All right, next question.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:19.950
If you take a walk

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:20.940
around the block,

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.492
you might run into Ethan and Maya--

00:01:23.492 --> 00:01:24.480
(buzzer rings)

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.487
- Hawke.
(audience cheers)

00:01:26.487 --> 00:01:28.380
- [Jackie] Yes!
- Okay, all right--

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.662
- [Howie] Wow--
- We get serious now.

00:01:29.662 --> 00:01:32.070
- [Jackie] It's a tie.
- [Howie] It's a tie.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.450
- Next question.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.610
At Family Game Night, there is no loss

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.020
when you're playing with Diana

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.670
and Tracee Ellis--
(buzzer rings)

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:39.960
- Oh!
- Who did first?

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.220
- Me?

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:43.956
- I used to be her opening act, Ross.

00:01:43.956 --> 00:01:45.510
- Yeah!
(audience cheers)

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:46.860
- I was Diana Ross' opening act!

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.120
- Mine didn't cycle out.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.340
I gotta get my cycling out.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:51.330
- Okay, ready?

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:52.620
Next question.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.530
Once I give you this clue,
you'll give me some thanks

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.114
if you know the last
name of Tom and Colin--

00:01:58.114 --> 00:01:59.280
(buzzer rings)

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.300
- Hanks!
(bell dings)

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.850
Hey, hey.
(audience cheers)

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.179
- Whoa, 2-2,

00:02:04.179 --> 00:02:06.990
are you showing me 2-2

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.072
or is he saying, "Fun"--
- It's tied up.

00:02:08.072 --> 00:02:11.207
It's 2-all, let's go y'all!
- "We're having fun."

00:02:11.207 --> 00:02:12.040
- It's 2-all.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.770
- All right, you ready
for the next question?

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.090
- I'm ready.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.095
- Be careful you're not sorely mistaken

00:02:17.095 --> 00:02:20.081
when you answer the name
of Sosie and Kevin--

00:02:20.081 --> 00:02:21.720
(buzzer rings)

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.329
- Bacon, Bacon.
(bell dings)

00:02:23.329 --> 00:02:25.170
(audience cheers)

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.460
She was great in "Smile."

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.230
Did you see "Smile?"

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:29.063
She was great,

00:02:29.063 --> 00:02:30.000
that's not a joke,

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.600
she was great in "Smile," the movie.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:35.730
- Yeah, I know.
- She was in the movie.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:36.563
She was in the movie.

00:02:36.563 --> 00:02:38.400
- Okay, all right, come on.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.020
- She was in a movie.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.810
- This clue is much more
than just some filler,

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.430
it leads the last name of Ben--

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.461
- Ben Stiller.

00:02:45.461 --> 00:02:46.535
- No!
(bell dings)

00:02:46.535 --> 00:02:47.707
Wait, no,
(audience cheers)

00:02:47.707 --> 00:02:49.220
you gotta say the question.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:50.181
- Did you look?

00:02:50.181 --> 00:02:51.450
- No, wait a minute,

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.560
no I didn't look,

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.052
but she said "filler" and,

00:02:54.052 --> 00:02:55.170
I didn't cheat!
- You're the host,

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:56.003
of course you looked!

00:02:56.003 --> 00:02:57.930
- But I didn't hear a rule
where you have to wait

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:58.830
for the question to end

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:00.090
if you figure it out.
- Can we get--

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.950
- You can't make up rules now.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.360
No, I'm winning,

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.193
and I'm the host

00:03:04.193 --> 00:03:05.670
and I don't care.
(Terry laughs)

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:06.507
- Next question--
- You can do what you want

00:03:06.507 --> 00:03:07.794
on "America's Got Talent,"

00:03:07.794 --> 00:03:09.840
I can do what I want here.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.300
Wait till you see the prize
I'm gonna give myself,

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.831
cause I'm the host.

00:03:13.831 --> 00:03:15.300
- Okay--
- I'm the host.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.120
- This one's got my
head feeling a bit itchy

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.100
cuz I'm thinking of Nicole and Lionel--

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.414
- Richie!
(bell dings)

00:03:21.414 --> 00:03:23.033
(audience cheers)

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:24.240
Okay, we don't have to wait?
- He didn't wait til the end

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:25.471
of the question.
- We don't have to wait?

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.319
- We didn't get to the end--

00:03:26.319 --> 00:03:27.330
- We don't have to wait anymore!

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:28.980
- We don't, but I'm still winning.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.900
I'm still winning.
(Terry laughs)

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.010
- All right, next one.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.470
Don't forget to repay all of your loans

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:37.740
if you owe money to Rashida and Quincy--

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.172
- Jones.
(bell dings)

00:03:39.172 --> 00:03:42.270
(audience cheers)

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.250
Sosie Bacon was in "Smile."

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:47.687
It's a horror movie.
(audience laughs)

00:03:47.687 --> 00:03:48.520
(air horn blows)

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:49.470
- Whoa!
- Aw!

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:50.970
- Excuse yourself!

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:52.200
Excuse yourself!

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.120
- Four or five points on this last one?

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.190
You get 10 points on the last one.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:58.200
- That means--
- She ate at a clown buffet

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.210
and it's upset her stomach.
(audience laughs)

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.790
- All right, this is your final question

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:04.470
and it's worth 10 points.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.730
- Yes!

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.203
- It's worth 10 points.

00:04:07.203 --> 00:04:08.850
- Yep, yep, yep.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.500
- So anyone can win.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.910
Everyone calm down,

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:12.900
don't have a cow,

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.295
it's all about Maude and Judd--

00:04:15.295 --> 00:04:16.558
- Apatow.
- Apatow, no!

00:04:16.558 --> 00:04:17.668
(bell dings)

00:04:17.668 --> 00:04:19.841
(horn blares)
(audience cheers)

00:04:19.841 --> 00:04:23.469
- Thank you, thank you.
(fanfare music)

00:04:23.469 --> 00:04:25.320
- Okay, okay.
- Nice!

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:26.153
- What do you win?

00:04:26.153 --> 00:04:27.720
What did you win?

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.432
- I win a podium.

00:04:30.432 --> 00:04:31.851
(Crews laughs)
(audience cheers)

00:04:31.851 --> 00:04:33.712
Thank you, thank you.

00:04:33.712 --> 00:04:34.984
You get a cardboard cutout.

00:04:34.984 --> 00:04:36.866
You can get a cardboard cutout of Kelly.

00:04:36.866 --> 00:04:41.866
I'll be taking the podium.
(audience applauds)

00:04:42.523 --> 00:04:44.580
I going to take this home.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:45.870
I wanna take this home.

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:48.240
Let's do a commercial and
I'm gonna get this unhooked.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:49.073
Thank you so much.

00:04:49.073 --> 00:04:49.906
We wanted one.

00:04:49.906 --> 00:04:50.739
My wife wants one

00:04:50.739 --> 00:04:52.467
for the end of the bed
in the master bedroom.

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:54.930
(Crews laughs)

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:56.430
Are we ready to begin?

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:59.220
Remember, listen to "Howie
Mandel Does Stuff" podcast

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.660
wherever you get your podcasts,

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:03.367
and watch "America's Got
Talent All Stars" on NBC.

